# Edge of the name-length rules (#724): a class of 1023 characters. Epic
# refuses one of 1024 (9002) and runs one of 960. OpenVerse admits names of
# a class up to 1023 characters and prints
#   field 42 | method 1
# If Epic refuses it, the class limit is lower (a prefix or suffix in its
# internal name). Run it alone (single mode).
# Epic's compiler (UEFN 43.12, ++Fortnite+Release-43.12-CL-60598086,
# BuildAll, 2026-11-19) refuses it: 3655 (L8) "Identifier is too long".
Class___ := class:
    V:int = 42
    F():int = 1

Main():void =
    Obj := Class___{}
    Print("OVPROBE field {Obj.V}")
    Print("OVPROBE method {Obj.F()}")
